# Prisma
/lib/generated/prisma
# migration_lock.toml is deliberately tracked, not ignored. It records which provider the
# migration history was written against, which is how Prisma catches this schema being
# pointed at a different engine. Ignoring it was harmless while there were no migrations;
# with a history in place and a move to Cloud SQL coming, it is the file that catches it.

# Playwright test screenshots
.playwright-mcp/
test-results/
playwright-report/

.vercel
.env*

# Transient UI captures, organized on disk but not worth versioning
docs/screenshots/
.playwright-mcp/

# Print-resolution brand assets: 17MB of sources the app does not serve.
# The derived email assets in public/email/ are the ones that ship.
public/link-linkroad logos/

# Screenshot artefacts. Playwright writes to the working directory when given a bare
# filename, so these accumulate at the root; real image assets live in subdirectories.
/*.png

# Working files for scripts/import-memes.ts: re-encoded JPEGs and the caption manifest.
# Intermediate output, regenerable from public/images/memes by re-running the dry run.
scripts/.meme-import/


# Written by .github/scripts/audit-gate.mjs, in CI and when running it by hand.
/audit.json
/audit-new.md
